AVX10.2: saturating byte converts (NaN response and element zero-extension), VMINMAX sign control on a NaN src1, BF16 FMA (single rounding, operand roles), VCOMXSS/VCOMXSD opmap swap, VCVT2PH2{B,H}F8 upper-half mask, VMOVRS mask rows

Eight defects found while diffing an independent model of the AVX10.2 group
against the emulator; each is pinned by the Intel AVX10.2 Architecture
Specification (361050-007) text quoted below.

1. VCVT[T]{PS,PH,BF16}2IBS wrote the converted signed byte SIGN-extended into
   its 32/16-bit element: the handler macros assign the int8_t result of
   f32_to_i8_saturate / f16_to_i8_saturate / bf16_to_i8_saturate to a Bit32u /
   Bit16u lane. The spec: "The downconverted 8-bit result is written in place
   at the lower 8-bit of the corresponding 32-bit element. The upper 3 bytes
   are zeroed" (and "The upper byte is zeroed" for the 16-bit forms). Every
   negative result was wrong (-1 became 0xFFFFFFFF instead of 0x000000FF).
   Fixed with zero-extending wrappers bound to the twelve signed handlers; the
   unsigned forms already returned a uint8_t.

2. f32_to_i8 / f32_to_ui8 (the ROUNDING converts behind VCVTPS2I[U]BS and
   VCVTBF162I[U]BS) skipped their NaN check entirely: the guard was written
   against the i32_/ui32_ specialize constants, which are all equal, so the
   whole #if block compiled out and a NaN fell through to the overflow path,
   returning +127/-128 (0xFF/0) by sign. The spec: "For NaN, (0) is returned"
   - as the truncating _r_minMag siblings and the f16 versions already do.
   Fixed by making the check unconditional like f16_to_i8.

3. f{16,32,64}_minmax with sign control 0b00 (take the sign of src1) copied
   src1's sign onto a NUMBER result when src1 was the NaN and the operation was
   a *Number variant (the NaN is discarded, the other operand returned). The
   spec: "The sign control indication ignores NAN signs: it does not manipulate
   the sign if the result is a NAN, and does not copy the sign of SRC1 (for
   sign control=0b00) if SRC1 is a NAN" (table 11.4: qNaN1/sNaN1 with Norm2 ->
   Norm2, "Imm8[3:2]==0b00 ignored"). Fixed by skipping case 0 when a is NaN.

4. bf16_mulAdd (all twelve VF[N]M{ADD,SUB}{132,213,231}BF16) rounded twice:
   f32_mulAdd rounded the exact a*b+c to 24 bits, convert_ne_fp32_to_bfloat16
   rounded again to 8. When the 16-bit exact product sits on a bf16 midpoint
   and the addend is smaller than half an f32 ulp of it, the first rounding
   loses the addend and the second rounds the tie to even where the true
   result was strictly above/below the midpoint. The spec describes the
   operation on "the negated infinite precision intermediate product" with
   RNE - one rounding. The other bf16 helpers are safe (an 8x8-bit product is
   exact in f32; a sum, quotient or square root of 8-bit operands can never
   land within f32 rounding distance of a bf16 midpoint), so only the FMA is
   changed: f32_mulAdd under round-to-zero with the inexact flag jammed into
   the result's LSB (round-to-odd at 24 bits), then the existing RNE narrowing
   - the classic exact double-rounding-free construction since 24 >= 8 + 2.

5. The twenty-four VF[N]M{ADD,SUB}{132,213,231}BF16 rows (plain and masked)
   were bound to HANDLE_AVX_3OP / HANDLE_AVX512_3OP_WORD_EL_MASK, the
   ACCUMULATE-shaped templates whose first lane operand is the DESTINATION
   register and which never read src3. The rows list their operands in the
   FMA3 role order the fp16 rows use (dst, src1, src2, src3), so every form
   computed the wrong product: 132 gave dst*dst+rm, 213 gave dst*vvvv+dst,
   231 gave dst*vvvv+rm (probe: dst=2, vvvv=3, rm=5 -> 9/8/11 instead of
   13/11/17). New HANDLE_AVX_3SRC / HANDLE_AVX512_3SRC_WORD_EL_MASK templates
   read src1/src2/src3 like HANDLE_AVX_PFP_3OP does, and the rows are rebound.

6. The EVEX 0F 2E / 0F 2F opmap rows swapped the two scalar-size AVX10.2
   compares: F3.W0 (the spec's VCOMXSS / VUCOMXSS encoding) dispatched
   VCOMXSD / VUCOMXSD and F2.W1 (VCOMXSD / VUCOMXSD) dispatched VCOMXSS /
   VUCOMXSS, so a `vcomxss` compared the low QWORDS as doubles: NaN vs 1.0
   came out "greater" (all flags clear) because 0x7FC00000 and 0x3F800000 are
   both tiny positive doubles. The IA names are swapped back; the handlers and
   the ia_opcodes_evex.def rows were already right.

7. VCVT2PH2BF8[S] / VCVT2PH2HF8[S] walk their 2*KL byte lanes with a Bit32u
   lane bit and a 32-bit opmask read. At VL512 there are 64 lanes: the lane
   bit shifts out after 32 iterations, so the upper half - every byte that
   comes from src1 - was never written and the destination kept its old
   bytes, masked or not. Bit64u and the 64-bit opmask read fix it.

8. The MAP5 6F opmap group (VMOVRS{B,W,D,Q}) carries ATTR_MASK_K0 on its
   _Kmask rows and no mask attribute on the plain rows - the reverse of every
   other group (ATTR_MASK_K0 marks the row that matches an ABSENT mask). A
   masked vmovrs therefore matched the plain row and ran the unmasked loader:
   `vmovrsd xmm1 {k7}, [mem]` with k7 = 0b0101 loaded all four dwords, {z}
   forms zeroed nothing. The attributes are moved to the plain rows.

Found 2026-09-14 by the hybrid-x86-oracle differential harness diffing the
zens model of the AVX10.2 group. All eight are present on upstream master as
of 2026-09-14.

The hunks below are deliberately comment-free apart from one-line notes, so
that this file can be sent upstream as-is.

